lders. Highwoods Properties, Inc., is headquarters in Raleigh. Highwoods Properties, Inc. was incorporated in 1978 in Maryland, USA.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Theodore J. Klinck | President, CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 315 people. Revenue per employee of $2.6M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers. Stock-based compensation of $26K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Highwoods Properties, Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $3.5B market cap on $806M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 9-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 3.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 3.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.07931454471289574},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 45% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","31 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Real Estate peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Reviewing Highwoods Properties (NYSE:HIW) & Brandywine Realty Trust (NYSE:BDN)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/reviewing-highwoods-properties-nysehiw-brandywine-realty-trust-nysebdn.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793999714.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.955,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Highwoods Properties (HIW) Earnings Beat Keeps Fair Value In Focus","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-hiw/highwoods-propert